+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# U2AC web UI
+
+A status and settings page for the dongle: one static `index.html` (inline CSS/JS, no external
+resources, about 32 KB) plus POSIX `sh` CGI scripts that use BusyBox applets only. BusyBox `httpd`
+serves it; nothing else is needed.
+
+## Starting it
+
+```sh
+httpd -p 10.0.0.1:80 -h /usr/share/u2ac/www        # on the AP, after `ip addr add 10.0.0.1/24 dev wlan0`
+httpd -p 192.168.50.2:80 -h /usr/share/u2ac/www    # on the USB (NCM) link, once usb0 has its address
+```
+
+- Run it as root: the CGIs write `/run/persist`, call `btmgmt`, `u2ac-aa`, `persist` and `reboot`.
+- `httpd` can bind only to an address that already exists, so start each instance after its address is up.
+- **Port clash:** the shipped `aa-proxy-rs.config.toml` has `webserver = "0.0.0.0:80"`. A wildcard
+  bind on :80 makes `httpd -p 10.0.0.1:80` fail (or the other way round). Set it to
+  `webserver = "0.0.0.0:8080"`: the About tab links to `http://<host>:8080/` as "Advanced (aa-proxy)".
+- Files: `cgi-bin/*` must be mode 0755, `cgi-bin/_lib.sh` mode 0644 (sourced, never run; `httpd` answers
+  404 for it).
+
+## Endpoints
+
+Every CGI prints `Content-Type: application/json` and a JSON object with `"ok"`. Failures are
+`{"ok":false,"error":"<text>","code":"<code>"}` with HTTP 200.
+
+| Endpoint | Method | What it returns or does |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cgi-bin/status` | GET | Dashboard object (polled every 3 s): `aa.state` (`off`, `waiting`, `connected`, `streaming`), `aa.last` (newest aa-proxy-rs log line), `mode.set` (`auto`, `dev`, `aa`) and `mode.active` (`aa`, `maint`), `svc.*` daemon booleans, `wifi` (ssid, channel, freq, width, txpower, `clients[]` with signal dBm, tx/rx bitrate, connected time, DHCP ip/host), `bt` (addr, name, powered, discoverable, paired count), `sys` (uptime, load, CPU kHz/max/governor, memory, `temp_mc` or null, build, kernel). |
+| `cgi-bin/logs?src=S&n=N` | GET | Last N lines (20 to 500, default 200), ANSI codes stripped. S: `aa` (`/var/log/aa-proxy-rs.log`, falls back to `/run/log/aa-proxy-rs.console`), `svc` (`/run/log/u2ac-aa.log`), `hostapd`, `bt` (`/run/log/bluetoothd.log`), `web` (`/run/log/u2ac-web.log`, this UI's own change log), `dmesg`. |
+| `cgi-bin/settings` | GET | Wi-Fi name (override, else config.toml, else hostapd.conf), the SSID the AP runs now, Bluetooth name, paired devices (`/var/lib/bluetooth/<adapter>/<device>/info`), startup mode, `pending_reboot`, whether `reboot-recovery` exists. Never the password. |
+| `cgi-bin/about` | GET | Versions (kernel, build, board, aa-proxy-rs, BlueZ, hostapd, iw, BusyBox; cached for the boot in `/run/u2ac-web/versions`) and cpufreq `time_in_state`. |
+| `cgi-bin/token` | GET | The access code, when this request may see it (see Security). |
+| `cgi-bin/action` | POST | Changes. Form-urlencoded body: `token=<code>&confirm=yes&action=<a>` plus fields below. |
+
+`action` values:
+
+| action | Fields | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| `wifi` | `ssid`, `psk`, `alias` (each optional, empty keeps the current value) | Rewrites the first `  ssid = "…"`, `  wpa_passphrase = "…"` and `  btalias = "…"` lines of `/etc/aa-proxy-rs/config.toml`, writes `/run/persist/u2ac-wifi.conf`, then `u2ac-aa persist` (or `persist save` when only the override changed). Applies after a reboot. |
+| `forget` | `dev=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF` or `dev=all` | `btmgmt -i hci0 unpair`, removes the device directory (and its `cache/` entry), then `u2ac-aa persist`. |
+| `mode` | `to=auto`, `maintenance` or `aa` | `u2ac-aa dev off`, `dev on` or `dev aa` (from the next boot). |
+| `aa-now` | | `u2ac-aa aa-now`. |
+| `reboot` | | `u2ac-aa persist`, then `reboot` 1 s after the reply. |
+| `recovery` | | Same with `reboot-recovery` (only if it is on PATH). |
+
+Input rules, checked again on the server: Wi-Fi name 1 to 32 printable ASCII characters, password 8 to 63,
+neither containing `"` or `\`; Bluetooth name 1 to 32 of `A-Z a-z 0-9 space _ -`; addresses
+`XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX` in upper-case hex. A body holding anything other than form-urlencoded characters is
+refused before decoding; decoded values outside printable ASCII are refused. User input is never
+`eval`ed or put in a `sed`/`awk` program: it is written with `printf '%s'` or passed through awk
+`ENVIRON`. One change runs at a time (`flock` on `/run/u2ac-web/action.lock`).
+
+## The Wi-Fi override file
+
+`/run/persist/u2ac-wifi.conf` (mode 0600, saved in the persistent store), exactly two lines:
+
+```
+SSID=<name>
+PSK=<password>
+```
+
+Contract for the reader (`u2ac-aa`, before it starts `hostapd`):
+
+- Read the values literally, the rest of the line after the first `=`. **Never source the file** (`.`):
+  the values may hold `$`, backticks, `;` and spaces.
+- Both keys are always written together; `PSK` is the WPA2 passphrase.
+- The same values are in config.toml, so aa-proxy-rs tells the phone the credentials the AP uses.
+  If the AP ignores the override, the phone is sent a password the AP does not accept.
+
+Wiring this needs a change to `ap_up` in `/usr/sbin/u2ac-aa`, for example right after `HC` is chosen:
+
+```sh
+W=$P/u2ac-wifi.conf
+if [ -s "$W" ]; then
+    S=$(sed -n 's/^SSID=//p' "$W" | head -n 1); K=$(sed -n 's/^PSK=//p' "$W" | head -n 1)
+    if [ -n "$S" ] && [ ${#K} -ge 8 ]; then
+        grep -v -e '^ssid=' -e '^wpa_passphrase=' "$HC" > /run/hostapd.conf
+        printf 'ssid=%s\nwpa_passphrase=%s\n' "$S" "$K" >> /run/hostapd.conf
+        HC=/run/hostapd.conf
+    fi
+fi
+```
+
+## Security
+
+The page is reachable only on the dongle's WPA2 AP and the USB link. On top of that, every POST to
+`cgi-bin/action` needs an access code:
+
+- 32 hex characters in `/run/persist/u2ac-webtoken` (0600), created by the first `GET cgi-bin/token`
+  when the file does not exist (atomically, so only one visitor gets it). It is persisted with the
+  next save of `/run/persist` (every change made here triggers one).
+- `cgi-bin/token` returns the code only to the request that created it, to clients on the USB link
+  (`REMOTE_ADDR` in 192.168.50.0/24), and once after `touch /run/u2ac-web/reveal-once` (over ssh).
+  Everyone else gets `null` and types the code in; the page keeps it in `localStorage`.
+- Mutations are POST only and also need `confirm=yes` (the page asks first). A cross-site form cannot
+  know the code, so it cannot make changes.
+- To change the code: `rm /run/persist/u2ac-webtoken` and open the page (or write 32 hex characters to it).
+
+## Testing on a host
+
+The scripts take `FAKE_ROOT` (prefix for every file path) and `FAKE_PATH` (directories put first on
+PATH, for stubs of `iw`, `btmgmt`, `u2ac-aa`, `persist`, `reboot`, `dumpleases`). With Docker:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm -p 127.0.0.1:18080:80 -v "$PWD":/www:ro -v <fake-root>:/fake -v <stubs>:/stubs:ro \
+    -e FAKE_ROOT=/fake -e FAKE_PATH=/stubs busybox:1.37 httpd -f -p 80 -h /www
+```
+
+The state shown is a heuristic: `streaming` means aa-proxy-rs is running, a Wi-Fi station is
+associated, and the newest session event in the last 120 log lines is `first video frame` (not
+followed by `session time:`, `closing session`, `disconnected phone`, `Terminated single session`,
+`ByeBye`, `session error` or `connection reset`).
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/_lib.sh b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/_lib.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..238ee65
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/_lib.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+# u2ac web UI: helpers shared by the CGI scripts (sourced, never executed; mode 0644 so httpd will not
+# run it). POSIX sh / BusyBox ash + BusyBox applets only. User input is never eval'd, never used in a
+# sed/awk program or a regex: it reaches files only through printf '%s' and awk ENVIRON[].
+#
+# FAKE_ROOT (host self-test only, unset on the unit): prefix for every file path, so the scripts can run
+# against a fake /proc, /sys, /run, /etc and /var tree. Commands (iw, btmgmt, u2ac-aa, persist, reboot,
+# dumpleases) are found on PATH, so a test puts stubs first on PATH.
+R=${FAKE_ROOT:-}
+P=$R/run/persist
+WEB=$R/run/u2ac-web
+TOKEN=$P/u2ac-webtoken
+WIFI_OVR=$P/u2ac-wifi.conf
+AACFG=$R/etc/aa-proxy-rs/config.toml
+BTLIB=$R/var/lib/bluetooth
+HAPCONF=$R/usr/share/u2ac/hostapd.conf
+LEASES=$R/run/udhcpd-wlan.leases
+SVCLOG=$R/run/log/u2ac-aa.log
+HAPLOG=$R/run/log/hostapd.log
+BTLOG=$R/run/log/bluetoothd.log
+AALOG=$R/var/log/aa-proxy-rs.log
+[ -s "$AALOG" ] || [ ! -s "$R/run/log/aa-proxy-rs.console" ] || AALOG=$R/run/log/aa-proxy-rs.console
+WEBLOG=$R/run/log/u2ac-web.log
+
+PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin${PATH:+:$PATH}
+[ -n "${FAKE_PATH:-}" ] && PATH=$FAKE_PATH:$PATH
+export PATH
+mkdir -p "$WEB" 2>/dev/null
+
+TO=; command -v timeout > /dev/null 2>&1 && TO="timeout 4"
+
+# btm ARGS: btmgmt with an open, empty FIFO as stdin. BlueZ 5.87's btmgmt reads a non-tty stdin as a command
+# script and quits at its EOF before the kernel's reply (a POST CGI's stdin is the drained body: an unpair
+# could be dropped); the same fix as u2ac-aa's bt_up. fd 9 (callers' locks) is not passed on.
+btm() {
+    _bf=$WEB/btmgmt.$$
+    rm -f "$_bf"
+    if mkfifo "$_bf" 2> /dev/null && exec 7<> "$_bf"; then
+        rm -f "$_bf"; $TO btmgmt "$@" 9>&- <&7; _br=$?; exec 7<&-
+    else
+        rm -f "$_bf"; $TO btmgmt "$@" 9>&- < /dev/null; _br=$?
+    fi
+    return $_br
+}
+
+# awk functions: rep (literal replace, no regex/backslash surprises), jesc (JSON string body)
+AWKLIB='
+function rep(s, f, t,   o, i) { o = ""; while ((i = index(s, f)) > 0) { o = o substr(s, 1, i - 1) t; s = substr(s, i + length(f)) } return o s }
+function jesc(s) { s = rep(s, "\\", "\\\\"); s = rep(s, "\"", "\\\""); gsub(/\t/, " ", s); gsub(/[\001-\037\177]/, "", s); return s }
+function js(s) { return "\"" jesc(s) "\"" }
+function noansi(s) { gsub(/\033\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-z]/, "", s); gsub(/\033[()][A-Z0-9]/, "", s); return s }
+'
+
+hdr() { printf 'Content-Type: application/json\r\nCache-Control: no-store\r\n\r\n'; }
+
+# jstr STRING: STRING as a JSON string literal (quotes included)
+jstr() { printf '%s' "$1" | awk "$AWKLIB"'BEGIN { ORS = ""; o = "" } { o = o (NR > 1 ? "\\n" : "") jesc($0) } END { print "\"" o "\"" }'; }
+
+# fail MESSAGE [CODE]: MESSAGE and CODE are fixed text from these scripts, never user input
+fail() { hdr; printf '{"ok":false,"error":%s,"code":"%s"}\n' "$(jstr "$1")" "${2:-error}"; exit 0; }
+
+now() { _up=; { read -r _up _ < "$R/proc/uptime"; } 2> /dev/null; NOW=${_up%%.*}; case $NOW in '' | *[!0-9]*) NOW=0 ;; esac; }
+
+# cache NAME TTL CMD...: refresh $WEB/NAME from CMD when older than TTL seconds (stamp = uptime, 1st line)
+cache() {
+    _cf=$WEB/$1 _ttl=$2; shift 2
+    if [ -s "$_cf" ]; then
+        { read -r _ _cts < "$_cf"; } 2> /dev/null
+        case $_cts in '' | *[!0-9]*) _cts=-99999 ;; esac
+        [ $((NOW - _cts)) -lt "$_ttl" ] && [ "$_cts" -le "$NOW" ] && return 0
+    fi
+    { echo "T $NOW"; "$@" 2> /dev/null; } > "$_cf.$$" && mv -f "$_cf.$$" "$_cf"
+}
+
+# query/body fields. qfield NAME -> $FV from QUERY_STRING (raw), field NAME -> $FV from the POST body (raw)
+qfield() { _q="&${QUERY_STRING:-}"; case $_q in *"&$1="*) FV=${_q#*"&$1="}; FV=${FV%%&*} ;; *) FV=; return 1 ;; esac; }
+field() { case "&$BODY" in *"&$1="*) FV="&$BODY"; FV=${FV#*"&$1="}; FV=${FV%%&*} ;; *) FV=; return 1 ;; esac; }
+
+read_body() {
+    [ "${REQUEST_METHOD:-}" = POST ] || fail "use POST" method
+    _n=${CONTENT_LENGTH:-0}
+    case $_n in '' | *[!0-9]*) _n=0 ;; esac
+    [ "$_n" -gt 4096 ] && fail "request too large" size
+    BODY=
+    [ "$_n" -gt 0 ] && BODY=$(head -c "$_n")
+    # the body itself is form-urlencoded: anything else in it is refused before any decoding
+    case $BODY in *[!A-Za-z0-9%+=\&._~*-]*) fail "malformed request" input ;; esac
+}
+
+# urldec RAW: form-urldecode; fails (no output) if the result would hold anything outside printable ASCII
+urldec() {
+    V=$1 awk 'BEGIN { s = ENVIRON["V"]; o = ""; h = "0123456789abcdef"; L = length(s)
+        for (i = 1; i <= L; i++) {
+            c = substr(s, i, 1)
+            if (c == "+") c = " "
+            else if (c == "%") {
+                a = index(h, tolower(substr(s, i + 1, 1))) - 1; b = index(h, tolower(substr(s, i + 2, 1))) - 1
+                if (a < 0 || b < 0) exit 1
+                n = a * 16 + b; if (n < 32 || n > 126) exit 1
+                c = sprintf("%c", n); i += 2
+            } else if (c < " " || c > "~") exit 1
+            o = o c
+        }
+        printf "%s", o }'
+}
+
+# validators (input already printable ASCII after urldec)
+valid_ssid() { [ ${#1} -ge 1 ] && [ ${#1} -le 32 ] && case $1 in *[\"\\]*) false ;; *) true ;; esac; }
+valid_psk() { [ ${#1} -ge 8 ] && [ ${#1} -le 63 ] && case $1 in *[\"\\]*) false ;; *) true ;; esac; }
+valid_alias() { [ ${#1} -ge 1 ] && [ ${#1} -le 32 ] && case $1 in *[!A-Za-z0-9\ _-]*) false ;; *) true ;; esac; }
+valid_mac() { case $1 in [0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]) true ;; *) false ;; esac; }
+
+# token: 32 hex chars in $P/u2ac-webtoken (0600), made on first use
+token_read() { TOK=; [ -s "$TOKEN" ] && read -r TOK < "$TOKEN"; case $TOK in *[!0-9a-f]* | '') TOK= ;; esac; }
+token_new() {
+    _t=$(tr -d '-' < /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid 2> /dev/null)
+    case $_t in ???????????????????????????????? ) ;; *) _t=$(od -An -N16 -tx1 /dev/urandom | tr -d ' \n') ;; esac
+    mkdir -p "$P" || return 1
+    # noclobber = O_EXCL: of two first visitors only one creates (and is shown) the token
+    (umask 077; set -C; printf '%s\n' "$_t" > "$TOKEN") 2> /dev/null
+}
+need_token() {
+    token_read
+    [ -n "$TOK" ] || fail "no access code exists yet: open the dashboard once to create it" token
+    field token || fail "this browser has no access code" token
+    [ "$FV" = "$TOK" ] || fail "wrong access code" token
+}
+# wireless interface: the first one with a phy80211 link in sysfs (never assumed), wlan0 if none is up yet
+wif() {
+    WIF=
+    for _w in "$R"/sys/class/net/*; do
+        [ -e "$_w/phy80211" ] && { WIF=${_w##*/}; break; }
+    done
+    : "${WIF:=wlan0}"
+}
+# REMOTE_ADDR: "a.b.c.d" on an IPv4 listener, "[::ffff:a.b.c.d]" on a dual-stack one
+from_usb() { _ra=${REMOTE_ADDR:-}; _ra=${_ra#[}; _ra=${_ra%]}; _ra=${_ra#::ffff:}; case $_ra in 192.168.50.*) true ;; *) false ;; esac; }
+
+weblog() { now; printf '%s web[%s]: %s\n' "$NOW" "${REMOTE_ADDR:-?}" "$*" >> "$WEBLOG" 2> /dev/null; }
+
+# tomlget KEY FILE: value of the first two-space-indented `KEY = "..."` line
+tomlget() {
+    K=$1 awk 'index($0, "  " ENVIRON["K"] " = \"") == 1 { s = substr($0, length(ENVIRON["K"]) + 7); i = index(s, "\""); while (i > 0 && substr(s, i - 1, 1) == "\\") { j = index(substr(s, i + 1), "\""); i = j ? i + j : 0 } print (i ? substr(s, 1, i - 1) : s); exit }' "$2" 2> /dev/null
+}
+# ovrget KEY: SSID or PSK from the override file (read literally, never sourced)
+ovrget() { K=$1 awk 'index($0, ENVIRON["K"] "=") == 1 { print substr($0, length(ENVIRON["K"]) + 2); exit }' "$WIFI_OVR" 2> /dev/null; }
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/about b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/about
